weak_answer:
The problem is that your `useEffect` is missing its **dependency array**. 

Without a dependency array, React runs the effect **after every single render**. Inside your effect, you call `setUser(...)`, which triggers a **re-render**. That new render runs the effect again, which calls `setUser`, causing an infinite loop:

$$\text{Render} \rightarrow \text{Effect runs} \rightarrow \text{setUser()} \rightarrow \text{Re-render} \rightarrow \text{Repeat...}$$

### The Fix

Pass `[id]` as the second argument to `useEffect`. This tells React: *"Only run this fetch when the `id` changes."*

```jsx
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

function Profile({ id }) {
  const [user, setUser] = useState(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    fetch(`/api/users/${id}`)
      .then(r => r.json())
      .then(setUser);
  }, [id]); // 👈 Added dependency array here

  return <div>{user?.name}</div>;
}
```

